description:
[narrowed from route-edit-135df0f0] Wire the first half of drafting-model grading. This change spans TWO files; apply BOTH edits.

FILE 1 — repos/llm-resolver-vessel/src/index.ts. Replace this line, which occurs exactly once:
  ["llmQuotaState", llmQuotaStateHandler as never],

with:
  ["llmArmOutcome_write", (async (ctx: { body: unknown }) => {
    const b = ctx.body as { model?: string; reached?: boolean; task_type?: string };
    if (!b || typeof b.model !== "string" || typeof b.reached !== "boolean") {
      return { resolved: false, shape: "llmArmOutcomeWriteResult", error: "body must include model as a string and reached as a boolean" };
    }
    await recordArmOutcome(b.model, b.reached, b.task_type);
    return { resolved: true, shape: "llmArmOutcomeWriteResult", body: { graded: b.model, reached: b.reached } };
  }) as never],
  ["llmQuotaState", (llmQuotaStateHandler) as never],

FILE 2 — repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/feature-compose.ts. Replace this line, which occurs exactly once:
  console.log("[fc-draft-model] selected=" + String((j as { model_selection?: { selected?: unknown } })?.model_selection?.selected ?? "unknown") + " task=feature_compose");

with:
  const __sel = String((j as { model_selection?: { selected?: unknown } })?.model_selection?.selected ?? "unknown");
  if (__sel !== "unknown") {
    (globalThis as Record<string, unknown>).__fcDraftModel = __sel;
    (globalThis as Record<string, unknown>).__fcDraftEndpoint = endpoint;
  }
  console.log("[fc-draft-model] pick=" + __sel + " task=feature_compose");

Why both are needed together: recordArmOutcome already maintains the per-task task_alpha and task_beta posteriors and already grades the seven task types that have them. Drafting (feature_compose, patch_with_tools) is excluded from immediate grading and the deferred grader was never wired, so those two task types carry ZERO learned posterior - model choice for authoring code rides on reputation earned at unrelated tasks. File 1 adds the shaped entry point through which an outcome can be reported. File 2 records which model drafted, and the endpoint to report to, so that entry point has a caller with real data. Neither half is meaningful alone.

WHY PREVIOUS ATTEMPTS ON THIS GAP FAILED (most recent last):
- dead_insertion_unwired: adversarial refuters agreed 2/2 (conf 0.90, 0.90): The patch does not genuinely close the gap because the `__fcDraftModel` and `__fcDraftEndpoint` global variables, which are intended to hold the mode

Do not repeat these failures. Address the specific cause named above.

